CallibriBird
Copyright 2026 Tykhyk Zolotarov

CallibriBird was created by Tykhyk Zolotarov. It is a muscle-rehabilitation
game: a patient plays Flappy Bird by squeezing a muscle, which a Callibri
sEMG sensor reads over Bluetooth, while the app records the muscle signal
and produces a session report.

Tykhyk Zolotarov's work in this project includes the whole EMG session
system: connecting the sensor, the person list, the guided meditation, the
rest and strength tests, calibration, controlling the game with a muscle,
the recording, the progress history and the HTML session report.

